pitalized Children Experiencing Anxiety\n\nDescription:\nAnxiety affects an estimated 7.1% (approximately 4.4 million) of children ages 3-17 in the United States yearly (Center for Disease Control and Prevention, 2021). Additionally, 200,000 children ages 14 and younger will visit an emergency room for playground-related injuries every year in the United States (Tinsworth, 2001). To create a resource that could help children decrease their hospital anxiety, studies were analyzed that focused on anxiety, hospitalization, coping strategies, and bibliotherapy. The findings found in these research studies were incorporated into the book. Additionally, five children's books were analyzed in order to review important factors seen in children's books for children ages 7-8. The first draft of the book was sent to be evaluated by the committee chair and then three external reviewers. They approved of the storybook and provided enthusiasm for the illustrations and how they came together with the story. The evaluators also provided feedback that enhanced the final draft of the book and made it more developmentally appropriate for the age group. The book was translated into Spanish and was then sent to be published on an online website called bookbilr.com. It was downloaded digitally for audience's accessibility. Future directions will include creating a glossary for children in the back of the book for children to have the opportunity to review vocabulary words. Additionally, creating a QR code that allows users to get access to the book is in plans for the future as well.\n\nEvaluate whether this book satisfies the user's search intent.\n\nReturn:\n\n* score (0, 1, or 2)\n* concise reason\n", 'role': 'user'}], 'model': 'gpt-4o-mini', 'response_format': {'type': 'json_schema', 'json_schema': {'schema': {'description': 'Structured relevance judgment for a single (query, book) pair.\n\nThe ``reason`` field is mandatory so every judgment can be audited\nor used for fine-tuning th