2026-06-11 20:38:02 | DEBUG    | openai._base_client | Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/chat/completions', 'headers': {'X-Stainless-Helper-Method': 'chat.completions.parse', 'X-Stainless-Raw-Response': 'true'}, 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-b7f2cf2e-d35c-4796-87e8-10e601905a58', 'post_parser': <function Completions.parse.<locals>.parser at 0x000001FC827622A0>, 'security': {'bearer_auth': True}, 'content': None, 'json_data': {'messages': [{'content': "You are a strict relevance judge for an information retrieval benchmark.\n\nYour task is to determine whether a candidate book satisfies the user's search intent.\n\nFocus on intent matching, not merely thematic similarity.\n\nScoring rubric:\n\n2 - HIGHLY RELEVANT\n\n* The book directly satisfies the query.\n* The main topic, genre, subject, setting, character type, or information need closely matches the query.\n* A user issuing this query would be very likely to click or select this book.\n\n1 - SOMEWHAT RELEVANT\n\n* The book has meaningful overlap with the query.\n* It shares some themes, genre, topics, or concepts.\n* However, it does not fully satisfy the query intent.\n* A user might consider the book as an alternative, but it is not an obvious match.\n\n0 - NOT RELEVANT\n\n* The book does not satisfy the query intent.\n* Similarity is weak, generic, incidental, or based only on broad genre overlap.\n* A user searching with this query would be unlikely to find the book useful.\n\nImportant guidelines:\n\n* Judge based on the query intent, not overall book quality.\n* Do not give score 1 simply because two books share a broad genre.\n* Prefer score 0 when overlap is weak or indirect.\n* Use score 2 sparingly and only for strong matches.\n* Be conservative when assigning relevance.\n\nAlways provide a concise reason (1-2 sentences).\n", 'role': 'system'}, {'content': "Search Query:\ntimeless fairy tales for kids\n\nCandidate Book:\n\nTitle: Spinning Gold\n\nDescription:\nUncover Rumpelstiltskin's untold tale: a misunderstood rogue, spinning more than just gold. Venture into the shadows of fairy tales, where villains are born, not made. Spinning Gold unravels the enigmatic life of Rumpelstiltskin, the notorious villain we all thought we knew. This retelling takes a daring twist, inviting us to step into his worn-out shoes and traverse the path that led him to his infamous deeds. The fairy-tale world is turned upside down as we journey into the heart of darkness, unearthing the origins of a character destined to be a villain. In the gleam of the original tale, Rumpelstiltskin is a fleeting presence, a mysterious helper who spins gold and vanishes, leaving behind a trail of enigma and awe. This timeless narrative, however, is about to be spun anew. Spinning Gold reels us into the depths of his existence, unspooling his story from his perspective. Here, Rumpelstiltskin is no longer just a supporting character in someone else's tale, but the leading figure of his own epic saga. While Rumpelstiltskin remains a villain, Spinning Gold provides a fresh perspective, reminding us that every character, no matter how wicked, has a backstory that deserves to be told. This unique narrative delves into the complexities of his character, revealing the layers of his life that drove him down the path of notoriety. Spinning Gold is more than just a retelling; it is a revelation, an unmasking of a character concealed in the shadows of fairy tales. This book invites you to suspend your preconceptions, hold on to your seats, and immerse yourself in the untold tale of Rumpelstiltskin. As you flip through its pages, you will find yourself questioning the line between hero and villain, between good and evil, and perhaps even between love and hate. So, are you ready to step into the shadows and uncover the truth? Are you prepared to spin a new understanding of villainy? If you are, then Spinning Gold awaits you. Experience the fairy tale world from a new pers\n\nEvaluate whether this book satisfies the user's search intent.\n\nReturn:\n\n* score (0, 1, or 2)\n* concise reason\n", 'role': 'user'}], 'model': 'gpt-4o-mini', 'response_format': {'type': 'json_schema', 'json_schema': {'schema': {'description': 'Structured relevance judgment for a single (query, book) pair.\n\nThe ``reason`` field is mandatory so every judgment can be audited\nor used for fine-tuning the judge model later.', 'properties': {'score': {'description': 'Relevance score: 0 = not relevant, 1 = somewhat relevant, 2 = highly relevant.', 'title': 'Score', 'type': 'integer'}, 'reason': {'description': 'Concise explanation (1-3 sentences) justifying the score. Used for auditing and debugging.', 'title': 'Reason', 'type': 'string'}}, 'required': ['score', 'reason'], 'title': 'RelevanceScore', 'type': 'object', 'additionalProperties': False}, 'name': 'RelevanceScore', 'strict': True}}, 'stream': False, 'temperature': 0.0}}
