scription:\n"The Crime at Black Dudley" by Margery Allingham is a gripping and suspenseful classic that introduces readers to one of her most beloved characters, Albert Campion. Set in an isolated English manor house, this intriguing mystery combines atmospheric tension with unexpected twists, keeping readers on the edge of their seats from start to finish. The story begins when a group of guests gathers for a weekend at Black Dudley, the home of the eccentric and wealthy Sir Reuben Levy. What was supposed to be a peaceful retreat quickly turns into a nightmare when a murder occurs during a late-night seance. As the guests find themselves trapped in the house due to a snowstorm, they must unravel the mystery of the crime before the killer strikes again. At the heart of the investigation is Albert Campion, a charming and unassuming gentleman with a knack for solving complex mysteries. With his calm demeanor and sharp intellect, Campion takes on the role of amateur detective, working alongside Scotland Yard to uncover the truth behind the murder. As the case deepens, Campion uncovers hidden motives, dark secrets, and unexpected alliances, all while navigating the tension-filled atmosphere of Black Dudley. "The Crime at Black Dudley" is a classic example of a locked-room mystery, where the sense of claustrophobia and isolation adds to the suspense. Allinghams clever plotting and engaging prose keep readers guessing, with red herrings and surprising revelations along the way. The novel also introduces a cast of colorful characters, each with their own secrets and hidden agendas, making it a thrilling ride for fans of traditional detective fiction. ABOUT THE AUTHOR Margery Allingham (19041966) was a British crime writer hailed as one of the Queens of Crime alongside Agatha Christie and Dorothy L. Sayers. Best known for her gentleman detective Albert Campion, Allinghams novels blend classic whodunit elements with rich characterization, wit, and a touch of adventure. Her works, includ\n\nEvaluate whether this book satisfies the user\'s search intent.\n\nReturn:\n\n* score (0, 1, or 2)\n* concise reason\n', 'role': 'user'}], 'model': 'gpt-4o-mini', 'response_format': {'type': 'json_schema', 'json_schema': {'schema': {'description': 'Structured relevance judgment for a single (query, book) pair.\n\nThe ``reason`` field is mandatory so every judgment can be audited\nor used for fine-tuning the judge model later.', 'properties': {'score': {'description': 'Relevance score: 0 = not relevant, 1 = somewhat relevant, 2 = highly relevant.', 'title': 'Score', 'type': 'integer'}, 'reason': {'description': 'Concise explanation (1-3 sentences) justifying the score. Used for auditing and debugging.', 'title': 'Reason', 'type': 'string'}}, 'required': ['score', 'reason'], 'title': 'RelevanceScore', 'type': 'object', 'additionalProperties': False}, 'name': 'RelevanceScore', 'strict': True}}, 'stream': False, 'temperature': 0.0}}
