on:\nWhen the Dead Remember is a haunting psychological thriller that explores the fragile boundaries between memory, grief, and obsession. After the death of matriarch Cherri Walder, her daughter Juniper is consumed by sorrow. But grief turns to something darker when, on the day of the funeral, Juniper discovers her husband\'s betrayal. As she tries to cope, her daughter, Roni, moves in to help-but the walls of their home feel different now. Uneasy. Observed. Juniper becomes forgetful. Distracted. She begins to question her own mind-and the trust she once placed in those closest to her. Someone is watching the Walder women. Someone who knows what they\'re hiding-and what they\'ve already forgotten. Told through multiple points of view, including anonymous chapters labeled only "Guess Who," this layered domestic suspense novel draws the reader into a chilling narrative of surveillance, deception, and unraveling sanity. When the Dead Remember delivers an atmospheric and psychologically rich story where grief distorts truth, and memory can\'t be trusted.\n\nEvaluate whether this book satisfies the user\'s search intent.\n\nReturn:\n\n* score (0, 1, or 2)\n* concise reason\n', 'role': 'user'}], 'model': 'gpt-4o-mini', 'response_format': {'type': 'json_schema', 'json_schema': {'schema': {'description': 'Structured relevance judgment for a single (query, book) pair.\n\nThe ``reason`` field is mandatory so every judgment can be audited\nor used for fine-tuning the judge model later.', 'properties': {'score': {'description': 'Relevance score: 0 = not relevant, 1 = somewhat relevant, 2 = highly relevant.', 'title': 'Score', 'type': 'integer'}, 'reason': {'description': 'Concise explanation (1-3 sentences) justifying the score. Used for auditing and debugging.', 'title': 'Reason', 'type': 'string'}}, 'required': ['score', 'reason'], 'title': 'RelevanceScore', 'type': 'object', 'additionalProperties': False}, 'name': 'RelevanceScore', 'strict': True}}, 'stream': False, 'temperature': 0.0}}
