SHE KNOWS WHAT HAPPENED. THEY\'RE COUNTING ON NO ONE BELIEVING HER. In beautiful Madrid, Irene hears her son calling out in the dark. She runs-only to be told she imagined it. The police don\'t open a case. The doctor increases her medication. Friends speak gently, like they\'re managing a crisis. And somewhere behind the official smiles, a quiet message keeps repeating: You\'re unstable. You\'re confused. You\'re not credible. But Irene knows what she heard. And she knows who wants her silent. The more she fights back, the worse it gets. Records don\'t match. Conversations vanish. Small "mistakes" pile up until her own memory feels like evidence against her. Then she spots the pattern-someone is pushing every lever designed to break a woman in public: discredit her, isolate her, and make the truth sound like paranoia. Because Irene isn\'t chasing a misunderstanding. She\'s circling a secret that reaches into places she can\'t touch... and people who don\'t lose. If she keeps digging, she risks losing everything: her reputation, her freedom-maybe even her life. But if she stops, her son disappears forever. The Woman They Silenced is a dark, addictive psychological thriller of gaslighting, betrayal, and an institutional cover-up-perfect for fans of twisty, high-tension suspense where the real terror is being told you can\'t trust your own mind. What readers are saying: "A tense psychological thriller with a mother at the center who refuses to be erased. The pacing is sharp, the dread feels real, and the Madrid setting adds grit instead of glamour. I finished it in two sittings." - Ray Thompson "Fast chapters, strong cliffhangers, and a mystery that keeps widening without getting confusing. The emotional core is what makes it hit: it\'s not just \'what happened, \' but what it costs. If you like dark, realistic conspiracies, this delivers." - Diane Brooks Start reading now-because once they decide you\'re "crazy," the truth becomes a weapon.\n\nEvaluate whether this book satisfies the user\'s search intent.\n\nReturn:\n\n* score (0, 1, or 2)\n* concise reason\n', 'role': 'user'}], 'model': 'gpt-4o-mini', 'response_format': {'type': 'json_schema', 'json_schema': {'schema': {'description': 'Structured relevance judgment for a single (query, book) pair.\n\nThe ``reason`` field is mandatory so every judgment can be audited\nor used for fine-tuning the judge model later.', 'properties': {'score': {'description': 'Relevance score: 0 = not relevant, 1 = somewhat relevant, 2 = highly relevant.', 'title': 'Score', 'type': 'integer'}, 'reason': {'description': 'Concise explanation (1-3 sentences) justifying the score. Used for auditing and debugging.', 'title': 'Reason', 'type': 'string'}}, 'required': ['score', 'reason'], 'title': 'RelevanceScore', 'type': 'object', 'additionalProperties': False}, 'name': 'RelevanceScore', 'strict': True}}, 'stream': False, 'temperature': 0.0}}
